420 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 213 0 R
/E (THE SEARCH FOR ALTERNATIVES TO CONVENTIONAL DAIRY )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
421 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 213 0 R
/E (French consumers are increasingly questioning standard cow's milk products, driven by health, digestibility, and environmental concerns. This takes multiple forms: a surge in plant-based alternatives \(oat, soy, almond\), with the French dairy alternatives market projected to reach $889 million by 2033 \(10.5% CAGR\); and a strong appetite for alternative animal milks, particularly goat and sheep products, which are growing rapidly especially among younger consumers seeking more natural and digestible options. Grand View Research, 2025)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
422 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 213 0 R
/E (VALUE FOR MONEY PRESSURE)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
423 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 213 0 R
/E (Despite easing inflation, French consumers remain price-conscious, making value for money a growing decision factor even in premium categories like cream and butter. This pressure is particularly strong among younger consumers.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
424 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 213 0 R
/E (SUSTAINABILITY EXPECTACTIONS)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
425 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 213 0 R
/E (Environmental concern is now one of the top issue for European consumers. Dairy brands are increasingly expected to demonstrate responsible sourcing, reduced carbon footprint, and ethical farming practices, or risk losing relevance.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [12]
>>
